These three files provide finite probability definitions and elementary
information identities. Local modifications change their import paths;
the upstream statements and proofs are retained. Their copyright headers
and license are preserved. This project proves the Mahdavifar–Beirami
argument in its own modules and does not import the upstream final theorem
or generated certificate collection.

Mathlib and its dependencies are separately fetched at the revisions in
lake-manifest.json and retain their respective notices and licenses.
The root Apache-2.0 license applies to the code in this repository; it does
not purport to change the license or authorship of the cited manuscript.
